 "__ENTITY__": "Page Builder",
 "doc_structure": "[{\"node\":\"menu_content105\",\"element\":\"menu_content\",\"data\":{\"label\":\"Docs Overview\",\"key\":\"docs_overview_menu_content\",\"id\":\"docs_overview_menu_content\",\"name\":\"docs_overview_menu_content\"},\"elements\":[{\"node\":\"markdown101\",\"element\":\"markdown\",\"data\":{\"label\":\"How Ren POS works\",\"key\":\"md_how_ren_pos_works\",\"id\":\"how-ren-pos-works\",\"name\":\"md_how_ren_pos_works\",\"value\":\"<style>\\n.rh-figure{margin:16px 0 24px}\\n.rh-figure svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;font-family:inherit;overflow:visible}\\n.rh-figure text{fill:hsl(var(--foreground));font-size:13px}\\n.rh-figure text.sm{font-size:11.5px}\\n.rh-figure text.lg{font-size:15px;font-weight:600}\\n.rh-figure text.b,.rh-figure tspan.b{font-weight:600}\\n.rh-figure .muted{fill:hsl(var(--muted-foreground))}\\n.rh-figure .box{fill:hsl(var(--card));stroke:hsl(var(--border));stroke-width:1.2}\\n.rh-figure .soft{fill:hsl(var(--muted));stroke:none}\\n.rh-figure .line{fill:none;stroke:hsl(var(--muted-foreground));stroke-width:1.4}\\n.rh-figure .dash{fill:none;stroke:hsl(var(--muted-foreground));stroke-width:1.2;stroke-dasharray:4 4}\\n.rh-figure .arrow{fill:hsl(var(--muted-foreground))}\\n.rh-figure .blue{fill:rgb(37 99 235 / .14);stroke:#2563eb;stroke-width:1.4}\\n.rh-figure .green{fill:rgb(22 163 74 / .14);stroke:#16a34a;stroke-width:1.4}\\n.rh-figure .orange{fill:rgb(234 88 12 / .14);stroke:#ea580c;stroke-width:1.4}\\n.rh-figure .red{fill:rgb(220 38 38 / .14);stroke:#dc2626;stroke-width:1.4}\\n.rh-figure .purple{fill:rgb(124 58 237 / .14);stroke:#7c3aed;stroke-width:1.4}\\n.rh-figure .t-blue{fill:#3b82f6}.rh-figure .t-green{fill:#22c55e}.rh-figure .t-orange{fill:#f97316}\\n.rh-figure .t-red{fill:#ef4444}.rh-figure .t-purple{fill:#8b5cf6}\\n.rh-figure .s-blue{stroke:#2563eb}.rh-figure .s-green{stroke:#16a34a}\\n</style>\\n\\n# How Ren POS works\\n\\nRen POS is a restaurant point of sale that runs inside ERPNext. Waiters take orders on tables, the kitchen and the bar work them on their own screens, and every paid order becomes an ERPNext **POS Invoice**: sales, taxes, payments and stock land in your books with no extra step.\\n\\n<figure class=\\\"rh-figure\\\">\\n<svg viewBox=\\\"0 0 760 360\\\" xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"How the parts of Ren POS fit together\\\">\\n<defs><marker id=\\\"ov-a\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 10 10\\\" refX=\\\"9\\\" refY=\\\"5\\\" markerWidth=\\\"7\\\" markerHeight=\\\"7\\\" orient=\\\"auto-start-reverse\\\"><path d=\\\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\\\" class=\\\"arrow\\\"/></marker></defs>\\n<!-- restaurant -->\\n<rect x=\\\"20\\\" y=\\\"20\\\" width=\\\"430\\\" height=\\\"320\\\" rx=\\\"14\\\" class=\\\"soft\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"40\\\" y=\\\"48\\\" class=\\\"lg\\\">Ren Restaurant</text>\\n<text x=\\\"40\\\" y=\\\"66\\\" class=\\\"sm muted\\\">a branch: menu, table policy, delivery, online ordering</text>\\n<!-- floor -->\\n<rect x=\\\"40\\\" y=\\\"82\\\" width=\\\"250\\\" height=\\\"236\\\" rx=\\\"10\\\" class=\\\"box\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"56\\\" y=\\\"106\\\" class=\\\"b\\\">Floor</text>\\n<rect x=\\\"56\\\" y=\\\"118\\\" width=\\\"218\\\" height=\\\"114\\\" rx=\\\"8\\\" class=\\\"blue\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"70\\\" y=\\\"140\\\" class=\\\"b t-blue\\\">Room</text>\\n<rect x=\\\"70\\\" y=\\\"152\\\" width=\\\"54\\\" height=\\\"34\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" class=\\\"box\\\"/><text x=\\\"85\\\" y=\\\"174\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">T-1</text>\\n<circle cx=\\\"160\\\" cy=\\\"169\\\" r=\\\"18\\\" class=\\\"box\\\"/><text x=\\\"149\\\" y=\\\"174\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">T-2</text>\\n<rect x=\\\"196\\\" y=\\\"152\\\" width=\\\"54\\\" height=\\\"34\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" class=\\\"box\\\"/><text x=\\\"211\\\" y=\\\"174\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">T-3</text>\\n<text x=\\\"70\\\" y=\\\"214\\\" class=\\\"sm muted\\\">tables hold the orders</text>\\n<rect x=\\\"56\\\" y=\\\"244\\\" width=\\\"218\\\" height=\\\"58\\\" rx=\\\"8\\\" class=\\\"orange\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"70\\\" y=\\\"266\\\" class=\\\"b t-orange\\\">Production centers</text>\\n<text x=\\\"70\\\" y=\\\"286\\\" class=\\\"sm muted\\\">kitchen, bar, expo: prepare items</text>\\n<!-- staff -->\\n<rect x=\\\"306\\\" y=\\\"82\\\" width=\\\"130\\\" height=\\\"110\\\" rx=\\\"10\\\" class=\\\"purple\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"320\\\" y=\\\"106\\\" class=\\\"b t-purple\\\">Ren Staff</text>\\n<text x=\\\"320\\\" y=\\\"128\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">who works here</text>\\n<text x=\\\"320\\\" y=\\\"146\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">their role</text>\\n<text x=\\\"320\\\" y=\\\"164\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">their floors, rooms,</text>\\n<text x=\\\"320\\\" y=\\\"180\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">tables and stations</text>\\n<rect x=\\\"306\\\" y=\\\"208\\\" width=\\\"130\\\" height=\\\"110\\\" rx=\\\"10\\\" class=\\\"box\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"320\\\" y=\\\"232\\\" class=\\\"b\\\">Menu</text>\\n<text x=\\\"320\\\" y=\\\"254\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">ERPNext Items</text>\\n<text x=\\\"320\\\" y=\\\"272\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">options, combos,</text>\\n<text x=\\\"320\\\" y=\\\"290\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">sizes, recipes</text>\\n<!-- ERPNext -->\\n<rect x=\\\"520\\\" y=\\\"20\\\" width=\\\"220\\\" height=\\\"320\\\" rx=\\\"14\\\" class=\\\"soft\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"540\\\" y=\\\"48\\\" class=\\\"lg\\\">ERPNext</text>\\n<text x=\\\"540\\\" y=\\\"66\\\" class=\\\"sm muted\\\">accounting and stock</text>\\n<rect x=\\\"540\\\" y=\\\"82\\\" width=\\\"180\\\" height=\\\"96\\\" rx=\\\"10\\\" class=\\\"green\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"556\\\" y=\\\"106\\\" class=\\\"b t-green\\\">POS Profile</text>\\n<text x=\\\"556\\\" y=\\\"128\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">who charges, payment</text>\\n<text x=\\\"556\\\" y=\\\"146\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">methods, price list,</text>\\n<text x=\\\"556\\\" y=\\\"164\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">taxes, warehouse</text>\\n<rect x=\\\"540\\\" y=\\\"196\\\" width=\\\"180\\\" height=\\\"56\\\" rx=\\\"10\\\" class=\\\"box\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"556\\\" y=\\\"220\\\" class=\\\"b\\\">POS Invoice</text>\\n<text x=\\\"556\\\" y=\\\"240\\\" class=\\\"sm muted\\\">one per paid order</text>\\n<rect x=\\\"540\\\" y=\\\"266\\\" width=\\\"180\\\" height=\\\"56\\\" rx=\\\"10\\\" class=\\\"box\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"556\\\" y=\\\"290\\\" class=\\\"b\\\">Stock Entry</text>\\n<text x=\\\"556\\\" y=\\\"310\\\" class=\\\"sm muted\\\">recipes, at register close</text>\\n<!-- arrows -->\\n<path d=\\\"M450 180 C 490 180, 500 224, 538 224\\\" class=\\\"line\\\" marker-end=\\\"url(#ov-a)\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"458\\\" y=\\\"170\\\" class=\\\"sm muted\\\">paid</text>\\n<path d=\\\"M630 178 L630 194\\\" class=\\\"line\\\" marker-end=\\\"url(#ov-a)\\\"/>\\n<path d=\\\"M630 252 L630 264\\\" class=\\\"line\\\" marker-end=\\\"url(#ov-a)\\\"/>\\n</svg>\\n</figure>\"}},{\"node\":\"markdown102\",\"element\":\"markdown\",\"data\":{\"label\":\"The pieces\",\"key\":\"md_the_pieces\",\"id\":\"the-pieces\",\"name\":\"md_the_pieces\",\"value\":\"# The pieces\\n\\n- **Restaurant** (Ren Restaurant): one branch. It holds the menu in force, the table policy, delivery and online ordering. If you have several branches, create one restaurant for each.\\n- **Floors, rooms and tables**: the floor plan you draw on the POS. Orders live on tables, including \\\"virtual\\\" tables such as *Delivery* or *Pickup* at the counter.\\n- **Production centers** (Ren Station): kitchen, grill, bar, expo, dispatch. Each one prepares some item groups and moves them through its own flow of statuses.\\n- **Staff** (Ren Staff): who works at each restaurant, with which **role** (Server, Cashier, Host, Kitchen, Manager…) and on which floors, rooms, tables and stations.\\n- **Menu**: the dishes and drinks are normal ERPNext **Items**. Options, combos, sizes and recipes are set on the Item, so ERPNext reports keep working.\\n- **POS Profile** (ERPNext): what charging uses: payment methods, price list, taxes, warehouse, and the cashiers who may charge with it.\"}},{\"node\":\"markdown103\",\"element\":\"markdown\",\"data\":{\"label\":\"The life of an order\",\"key\":\"md_the_life_of_an_order\",\"id\":\"the-life-of-an-order\",\"name\":\"md_the_life_of_an_order\",\"value\":\"# The life of an order\\n\\n<figure class=\\\"rh-figure\\\">\\n<svg viewBox=\\\"0 0 760 200\\\" xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"The life of an order\\\">\\n<defs><marker id=\\\"ol-a\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 10 10\\\" refX=\\\"9\\\" refY=\\\"5\\\" markerWidth=\\\"7\\\" markerHeight=\\\"7\\\" orient=\\\"auto\\\"><path d=\\\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\\\" class=\\\"arrow\\\"/></marker></defs>\\n<rect x=\\\"10\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" width=\\\"130\\\" height=\\\"78\\\" rx=\\\"10\\\" class=\\\"blue\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"24\\\" y=\\\"64\\\" class=\\\"b t-blue\\\">Waiter</text>\\n<text x=\\\"24\\\" y=\\\"84\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">opens the table,</text>\\n<text x=\\\"24\\\" y=\\\"100\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">adds items</text>\\n<rect x=\\\"164\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" width=\\\"128\\\" height=\\\"78\\\" rx=\\\"10\\\" class=\\\"box\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"178\\\" y=\\\"64\\\" class=\\\"b\\\">Send</text>\\n<text x=\\\"178\\\" y=\\\"84\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">items go to their</text>\\n<text x=\\\"178\\\" y=\\\"100\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">production centers</text>\\n<rect x=\\\"316\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" width=\\\"160\\\" height=\\\"78\\\" rx=\\\"10\\\" class=\\\"orange\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"330\\\" y=\\\"64\\\" class=\\\"b t-orange\\\">Production</text>\\n<text x=\\\"330\\\" y=\\\"84\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">Sent → Processing →</text>\\n<text x=\\\"330\\\" y=\\\"100\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">Completed → Delivered</text>\\n<rect x=\\\"500\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" width=\\\"116\\\" height=\\\"78\\\" rx=\\\"10\\\" class=\\\"box\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"514\\\" y=\\\"64\\\" class=\\\"b\\\">Bill</text>\\n<text x=\\\"514\\\" y=\\\"84\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">printed check,</text>\\n<text x=\\\"514\\\" y=\\\"100\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">split if needed</text>\\n<rect x=\\\"640\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" width=\\\"110\\\" height=\\\"78\\\" rx=\\\"10\\\" class=\\\"green\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"654\\\" y=\\\"64\\\" class=\\\"b t-green\\\">Pay</text>\\n<text x=\\\"654\\\" y=\\\"84\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">POS Invoice,</text>\\n<text x=\\\"654\\\" y=\\\"100\\\" class=\\\"sm\\\">order Invoiced</text>\\n<path d=\\\"M140 79 L160 79\\\" class=\\\"line\\\" marker-end=\\\"url(#ol-a)\\\"/>\\n<path d=\\\"M292 79 L312 79\\\" class=\\\"line\\\" marker-end=\\\"url(#ol-a)\\\"/>\\n<path d=\\\"M476 79 L496 79\\\" class=\\\"line\\\" marker-end=\\\"url(#ol-a)\\\"/>\\n<path d=\\\"M616 79 L636 79\\\" class=\\\"line\\\" marker-end=\\\"url(#ol-a)\\\"/>\\n<path d=\\\"M75 118 C 75 170, 380 170, 380 122\\\" class=\\\"dash\\\" marker-end=\\\"url(#ol-a)\\\"/>\\n<text x=\\\"140\\\" y=\\\"176\\\" class=\\\"sm muted\\\">more rounds: add items and Send again at any time</text>\\n</svg>\\n</figure>\\n\\n1. A waiter taps a table, adds items and taps **Send**. Each item goes to the production center that prepares its item group, and its ticket prints there if the station has a printer.\\n2. The kitchen moves items through its flow (for example *Sent → Processing → Completed*). The waiter sees each line's status live.\\n3. When the guests are done the waiter prints the **Bill** and someone with charging rights takes the payment, with tip and split check if needed.\\n4. The payment creates the POS Invoice and the order is closed. When the cashier closes the register, the shift becomes a POS Closing Entry and the recipe ingredients leave stock.\"}},{\"node\":\"markdown104\",\"element\":\"markdown\",\"data\":{\"label\":\"Where to start\",\"key\":\"md_where_to_start\",\"id\":\"where-to-start\",\"name\":\"md_where_to_start\",\"value\":\"# Where to start\\n\\n- First time? Follow the [setup checklist](/Docs/Setup%20Checklist).\\n- Looking for a screen? See [Taking orders](/Docs/Taking%20Orders), [Kitchen screen](/Docs/Kitchen%20Screen) or [Host stand](/Docs/Host%20Stand).\\n- Every guide is also reachable from the **Help** button on Ren forms and from the staff menu of the POS.\"}}]}]"
}
